Approved:, Rejected: and Superseded-by: now set tags on the list, but
only the hook's comments say how to write them, and a trailer written
slightly wrong is ignored without a word. A wrapped line without an
indent, for one, voids every trailer in the block. Writing the
protocol down next to the indexing rules lets a reviewer get it right
the first time, and says what each key means so that the tags mean the
same thing to everyone.
