+* Status trailers
+The state of a series is written on the list, in trailers at the end
+of a reply. The indexer derives a tag from each one, so the state
+comes back whenever the database is rebuilt. Nobody tags a thread by
+hand.
+
+A trailer is a =Key: value= line in the last paragraph of the
+message, as =git interpret-trailers --parse= finds it:
+
+#+BEGIN_SRC
+Thanks, this is what I wanted.
+
+Approved:
+#+END_SRC
+
+The rules:
+- Trailers go in the last paragraph, below everything else you
+  write. A signature below them, after a =--= line, is fine.
+- Every line of that paragraph must be a trailer or a continuation.
+  One other line voids the whole block, and no trailer counts.
+- Quoted lines never count, so quoting someone's trailer does not
+  repeat it.
+- Keys match without regard to case.
+- A value may continue on following lines that begin with a space or
+  tab. git joins them into one line. A paragraph wrapped without that
+  indent is not a trailer, so indent continuation lines or put a long
+  explanation in the prose above:
+
+#+BEGIN_SRC
+Rejected: the hook belongs in the mail workspace, where
+  the list is indexed
+#+END_SRC
+
+The keys:
+- =Superseded-by: id:<message-id>= :: the thread this message sits in
+  is replaced by the named message, usually the cover letter of the
+  new series. Use it when a different series replaces this one.
+- =Approved:= :: the thread is approved as-is. The value is optional
+  and free, e.g. thanks or an idea for follow-up. It never adds a
+  condition; approval with a condition is not yet approval.
+- =Rejected: <reason>= :: the thread is rejected. Give the reason,
+  e.g. =Rejected: withdrawn, scope moved to <subject>=.
+
+Each applies to the whole thread the reply sits in, not only the
+message it answers. Approved and rejected exclude each other: the
+latest message with either wins, and within one message the last
+trailer does. Anyone may write a trailer.
+
+A revised series needs no trailer. Its cover letter, or its only
+patch, ends with a =- Link to v(N-1): id:<message-id>= line, and the
+thread it names is superseded.
+
+The indexer sets these tags:
+- ~superseded~ :: a Link to vN line or a Superseded-by names the thread
+- ~approved~ :: the thread's latest verdict is Approved
+- ~rejected~ :: the thread's latest verdict is Rejected
+
+The sample notmuch config hides superseded threads through
+=search.exclude_tags=, and a search naming the tag still finds them.
+Approved and rejected threads stay visible; filter them in a search,
+e.g. =tag:inbox and not tag:rejected=.
